\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces Canonical checkpoint registry. 70 planned training runs, all 70 completed training. ``Beam-3 evaluation'' means a run was beam-3 decoded on at least the development set; of these 70 runs, 43 also have a canonical PHX-public PURE--REC gap under the \S  \ref  {sec:retrieval} donor registry (the remaining 27 were beam-3 evaluated on dev only and lack a canonical PHX-public PURE--REC gap). The 43 decoded runs reduce to 42 unique weight binaries: the long-schedule seed-202 artifact is byte-identical to the config-faithful seed-202 artifact (same wandb run, identical per-step losses, identical best-checkpoint SHA-256) and counts once. 67 non-holdout runs have dev metrics; 52 of these are non-distillation and enter the competence gate. 42 unique runs have both dev BLEU-4 and PHX-public PURE--REC gap (extrapolation-eligible). Plus the released original. Each family row's columns sum to the Total row.\relax }}{21}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:checkpoint_registry}{{S3}{21}{Canonical checkpoint registry. 70 planned training runs, all 70 completed training. ``Beam-3 evaluation'' means a run was beam-3 decoded on at least the development set; of these 70 runs, 43 also have a canonical PHX-public PURE--REC gap under the \S \ref {sec:retrieval} donor registry (the remaining 27 were beam-3 evaluated on dev only and lack a canonical PHX-public PURE--REC gap). The 43 decoded runs reduce to 42 unique weight binaries: the long-schedule seed-202 artifact is byte-identical to the config-faithful seed-202 artifact (same wandb run, identical per-step losses, identical best-checkpoint SHA-256) and counts once. 67 non-holdout runs have dev metrics; 52 of these are non-distillation and enter the competence gate. 42 unique runs have both dev BLEU-4 and PHX-public PURE--REC gap (extrapolation-eligible). Plus the released original. Each family row's columns sum to the Total row.\relax }{table.caption.9}{}}
